{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQ6AGoVmLHYZ9g3uWh7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `watch::Receiver::mark_unchanged()` in `tokio/src/sync/watch.rs`. It's the reverse of `mark_changed`: it sets the receiver's version to the channel's current version, so the current value counts as seen without being borrowed. After calling it, `has_changed()` returns `false` and `changed()` waits for the next send.\n\nI added a `rx_mark_unchanged` test to `tokio/tests/sync_watch.rs`. It checks two cases: undoing a `mark_changed()`, and dismissing a value that was really sent.\n\nGATE PASS: the new test fails without the source change and passes with it, and the format and leftover-debug checks are clean. I only ran the `rx_mark*` tests, not the full test suite. I also didn't add a doc-test example; the neighbouring `mark_changed` doesn't have one either."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":537,"cache_read_input_tokens":33423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":537,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":283,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e15166f-25a1-4b69-9f1b-fa6b581bd119","uuid":"a5660c34-3d14-4507-9768-d586a2983451","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:18:04.638Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQ6A3uXyb8dmTH3VQdx"}
